  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Given that $p\\propto\\frac{1}{q^3}$, what is the effect, correct to two decimal places, on:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p12-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$p$ when $q$ is increased by $10\\%$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$p$ decreases by approximately $24.87\\%$.",
          "worked": "Write $p=\\frac{k}{q^3}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}p_{\\text{new}}&=\\frac{k}{(1.1q)^3}\\\\p_{\\text{new}}&=\\frac{1000}{1331}p.\\end{align*}$$\nThe percentage decrease is\n$$\\left(1-\\frac{1000}{1331}\\right)\\times100\\%\\approx24.87\\%.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$p$ when $q$ is decreased by $10\\%$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$p$ increases by approximately $37.17\\%$.",
          "worked": "Write $p=\\frac{k}{q^3}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}p_{\\text{new}}&=\\frac{k}{(0.9q)^3}\\\\p_{\\text{new}}&=\\frac{1000}{729}p.\\end{align*}$$\nThe percentage increase is\n$$\\left(\\frac{1000}{729}-1\\right)\\times100\\%\\approx37.17\\%.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$q$ when $p$ is increased by $20\\%$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$q$ decreases by approximately $5.90\\%$.",
          "worked": "Since $pq^3=k$,\n$$\\begin{align*}1.2p\\,q_{\\text{new}}^3&=pq^3\\\\q_{\\text{new}}^3&=\\frac56q^3\\\\q_{\\text{new}}&=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac56}\\,q.\\end{align*}$$\nThe percentage decrease is\n$$\\left(1-\\sqrt[3]{\\frac56}\\right)\\times100\\%\\approx5.90\\%.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q14-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$q$ when $p$ is decreased by $20\\%$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$q$ increases by approximately $7.72\\%$.",
          "worked": "Since $pq^3=k$,\n$$\\begin{align*}0.8p\\,q_{\\text{new}}^3&=pq^3\\\\q_{\\text{new}}^3&=\\frac54q^3\\\\q_{\\text{new}}&=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac54}\\,q.\\end{align*}$$\nThe percentage increase is\n$$\\left(\\sqrt[3]{\\frac54}-1\\right)\\times100\\%\\approx7.72\\%.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      }
    ]
  },
